 # Changelog
 
-## [Unreleased]
+## [18.12.0-ojak.1]
+
+### Added
+
+- Extensions can durably save the first user turn with `ctx.persistSession()` and continue explicitly unsent context with `ctx.resumePendingTurn()` without duplicating user messages or tool effects.
+- Extensions can delay child creation with the cancellable, timeout-free `before_subagent_admission` hook inside existing subagent scheduling limits.
+- Provider extensions can identify the exact live request owner with readonly `ctx.providerSessionId` and distinguish primary from ephemeral requests through `options.requestKind`.
+- External request fences use stable-storage synchronization rather than ordinary buffered session flushes; unsupported storage fails closed before dispatch.
+
+### Fixed
+
+- Requests marked `execution_unknown` or `BRIDGE_EXECUTION_UNKNOWN` no longer trigger automatic retry, fallback, or continuation.
+- Paused or stopped admission no longer triggers automatic recovery; explicit resumption of a proven-unsent, output-free pause preserves the original user and completed tools.
 
